=== A. Rule 144 affiliate three-month volume cap ===
1% of 100000000 outstanding = 1000000
four-week average weekly volume = 1000000
listed-stock cap (greater of 1% and four-week average) = 1000000
if four-week average is 1500000, listed-stock cap = 1500000
OTC / non-listed: the SEC Rule 144 investor publication says only the 1% measure applies
OTC cap in this toy = 1000000 (1% only)
=== B. Form 144 notice threshold ===
  4000 shares at $10.00 (gross $40000): Form 144 required? False
  4000 shares at $20.00 (gross $80000): Form 144 required? True
  6000 shares at $5.00 (gross $30000): Form 144 required? True
  5000 shares at $10.00 (gross $50000): Form 144 required? False
Form 144 is a notice of proposed sale, filed with the order; it is not executed volume
=== C. Rule 105 restricted period (five business days before pricing) ===
pricing 2026-06-12; five business days before = 2026-06-05 (toy weekdays only)
  short on 2026-06-04: inside restricted period? False
  short on 2026-06-05: inside restricted period? True
  short on 2026-06-12: inside restricted period? True
a short inside this window plus a purchase of the offered shares from an underwriter is the Rule 105 prohibition (firm-commitment equity offerings); exceptions exist but are not modelled here
=== D. Rule 14e-1 minimum tender window (toy weekday count) ===
official 'business day' is defined in Rules 14d-1(g)(3) and 13e-4(a)(3); this toy counts Mon-Fri and ignores holidays
offer first published 2026-03-02; 20th weekday (counting that date as day 1) = 2026-03-27
if consideration is increased on 2026-03-20, 10 weekdays from that notice (counting that date as day 1) = 2026-04-02
the April 16, 2026 exemptive order can shorten some equity offers to 10 business days only when every stated condition is met; this toy does not apply that order
assertions passed: 15/15
=== E. Regulation M Rule 101/102 restricted period and shelf takedowns ===
  ADTV $500,000 and public float $80,000,000 -> 1-business-day restricted period
  ADTV $50,000 and public float $10,000,000 -> 5-business-day restricted period
  pricing before the close on 2026-06-09 (Tuesday); 1-day period requires a full trading day
  restricted period begins prior to the opening on 2026-06-08 (Monday), not at Monday's close
  ADTV for a delayed / Rule 415 offering is measured in the two full calendar months preceding,
  or any 60 consecutive calendar days ending within 10 calendar days preceding, pricing
  shelf: a shareholder with shares on a shelf who plans periodic sales does not stay in Rule 102
  from registration until the last share is sold; analyze each takedown to see whether it is a distribution
  shares registered on a shelf, this takedown is not a distribution -> in Rule 102 now? False
  ATM (Rule 100) means an offering of securities at other than a fixed price; no special ATM clock
  Rule 101 bars distribution participants (and affiliated purchasers) from bidding for or purchasing
  a covered security in the restricted period; if that person is the issuer or selling security holder, Rule 102 applies instead
  Rule 101 actively-traded exception (ADTV $1 million and public float $150 million) may not be used
  by a distribution participant who is an affiliate of the issuer; do not copy it onto the issuer under Rule 102
  exceptions exist; this toy is not a compliance engine. Rule 105 (short-then-buy-the-offering) stays as already taught
assertions passed: 19/19
=== F. Rule 14e-5: purchases outside a tender offer ===
official clock runs from public announcement until the tender offer expires, not only from formal commencement
announced 2026-03-02, expires 2026-03-27 (same toy window as section D)
  covered person, day of public announcement, market purchase: prohibited? True
  covered person, mid-offer market purchase: prohibited? True
  covered person, purchase as part of the tender offer: prohibited? False
  covered person, subsequent offering period, same consideration: prohibited? False
  covered person, after expiration, no subsequent period: prohibited? False
  person who is not a covered person, mid-offer: prohibited? False
the subsequent-offering-period carve-out applies only if the consideration is the same in form and amount; this toy does not invent a broader post-expiration trading rule
related securities = immediately convertible into, exchangeable for, or exercisable for subject securities
paragraph (b) exceptions exist (including certain pre-announcement contract purchases, specified covering transactions, and a 20-security basket with a 5% value cap); this toy does not build that engine
14e-1's minimum duration is not permission for a covered person to buy the subject or related securities in the market
assertions passed: 25/25
